course: dictionary
lesson: 4503
title: Hay and hay fever
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Hay is long grass that has been cut and dried. Farmers make it in summer and store it for winter, when grass will not grow. Horses, cows, rabbits and guinea pigs all eat hay.
explain: «A rabbit's teeth grow all its life; without enough hay to chew they can grow into sharp spikes that cut the mouth.» The clues are grow and chew: a rabbit's teeth keep growing, and chewing hay wears them down. So hay is something a rabbit needs to chew every day.
explain: Hay fever sounds like it is caused by hay, but it is not. «Hay fever is an allergy to pollen» from grass and plants, and it makes you sneeze and have itchy eyes. Try the test: if you swap in "hay causes it" and it does not fit the facts, your first guess was wrong.
fact: Hay is grass that has been cut and dried.
fact: Hay is uncountable, so you say some hay, not a hay or two hays.
fact: «Haymaking» means cutting grass, drying it in the sun, turning it and baling it for winter.
fact: «Hay fever» means an allergy to pollen, which causes sneezing, itching and a runny nose. It is not caused by hay and is not a fever.
fact: «Make hay while the sun shines» means use a good chance while you can. «Like a needle in a haystack» means very hard to find.
exercise: What is hay? | Thin sticks used to light a fire | *Long grass that has been cut and dried, to feed animals | A kind of sweet, dried fruit | Mud from a wet field
exercise: «Without enough hay to chew they can grow into sharp spikes.» Why do rabbits need hay? | To stop them hopping | To make them sneeze | To wrap their dinner in | *To chew, so their teeth do not grow into sharp spikes
exercise: Ella has hay fever. What causes it? | A fever she caught from a friend | *An allergy to pollen from grass and plants | Hay itself, so she must stay away from farms | A cold, like a cough
test: «Haymaking is cutting grass, drying it in the sun, turning it and baling it for winter.» What must happen before the grass is baled? | Painting it green | *It must be cut and dried in the sun | Freezing it in a bag
test: Why is wet hay a problem? | *Wet hay goes mouldy, and damp hay can get hot and even catch fire | Wet hay turns into grass again | Wet hay tastes sweeter, so animals love it | Wet hay is cheaper to buy
exam: «Make hay while the sun shines» means what? | Sunbathe in a field all day | Hide in a haystack until the sun goes down | *Use a good chance while you can | Cut grass in the sunshine only
